<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31250" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nŏtus</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nŏtos</span></b> , i, m.
		
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νότος</span>
		, = auster, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the south wind</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tres Notus hibernas immensa per aequora noctes
					Vexit me violentus aquā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 6, 355</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">madidis Notus evolat alis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					1, 264</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">udus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					Epod. 10, 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">procellosus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
					2, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tepidus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Am. 1, 4, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sub Noton et Borean,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					7, 363</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Poet.</b>, transf., for <i>wind</i> in gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tendunt vela Noti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 3, 268</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1</span></i>. 575; 5, 512;
				<i><span class="en">Tib.
				1, 5, 35</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
